format 1

# age-plugin-se's registry: every tracked file type and the hk steps that
# check it (root T6). Seeded by `pklith seed --init`; edited by hand since,
# one check per commit (paradigm/V21), in the order `pklith lay` lays them.
#
# The `## checks` rows are this repository's own. Swift and XCTest come from
# the host Xcode (D21), which the catalog's `nix` column cannot name
# (pklith#89), so the toolchain, build and test rows name no nix package and
# run what is on PATH; the shell's guard put the host Xcode there (nix V1),
# and the toolchain step runs that guard again on every commit.
#
# `bats-unit` replaces the catalog row: the specs sit beside their scripts
# in gate/ and release/, and on macOS's case-insensitive disk the catalog's
# `bats --recursive tests` opens the XCTest dir Tests/ and passes on 0
# tests. `bats-changed` runs a changed script's spec, found through the
# `gate-bats` and `release-bats` rules; `bats-unit` runs them all.
#
# `mth-fmt` replaces the catalog row to read SPEC-ARCHIVE.md files too:
# `mth archive` rewrites each archive's header hard-wrapped on every run,
# and the catalog row's `**/SPEC.md` glob let that drift land unseen.
# `mth check` stays SPEC.md only: an archive is a sink whose citations
# point into its SPEC.md, so it would report every one as dangling.
#
# `coverage` runs gate/coverage.sh, which skips with a notice below macOS
# 26: the floor was measured where the ML-KEM-768 tests run, and they
# skip on older macOS, so CI and macOS 26 hosts hold it (root V10).
#
# Not laid, each with its reason (root T6):
# - swiftlint: the seeded `.swiftlint.yml` finds 120 violations in upstream
#   code, which is not reformatted (D3, D13); it waits for the owner's
#   baseline convention (root V9, T18).
# - itok: `.context-limits` holds sherd's chain ceilings (paradigm/V12);
#   itok reads the same file as per-file ceilings and refuses SPEC.md at
#   3,563 tokens against its 2,900 chain ceiling.
# - actionlint, zizmor, yamllint on upstream `.github/` files: upstream CI
#   is untouched (root §C); they read the fork CI, `ci.yml`, only (T14).
# - the name guard's allowlist half (paradigm/V37): CI, which has no
#   denylist, would check every repository named or linked against a
#   committed list of public ones; the text already names third-party
#   repositories, so which go on that list is the owner's call (T19).

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|.githooks/*, .envrc, **/*.sh|shellcheck --shell=bash {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
mth-fmt|lint|-|**/SPEC.md, **/SPEC-ARCHIVE.md|(for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt --check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|(for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|-|a SPEC.md or SPEC-ARCHIVE.md is hard-wrapped or over the line cap; after `mth archive`, run `mth fmt` on the archive
build|lint|-|**/*.swift, Package.swift, Package.resolved|swift build --build-tests -Xswiftc -warnings-as-errors|-|-|the build or a compiler warning failed (root V7)
test|test|-|**/*.swift, Package.swift, Package.resolved, nix/test.sh|nix/test.sh swift|-|-|a test failed (root V15, nix V2)
hardware|test|-|**/*.swift, Package.swift, Package.resolved|test -n "${CI:-}" && echo 'hardware: CI is set, so the Secure Enclave suite is not run here (Tests §I)' \|\| AGE_PLUGIN_SE_HARDWARE=1 swift test --filter CryptoKitHardwareTests|-|-|a Secure Enclave hardware test failed on this Mac (Tests §I, root V15)
universal|test|-|**/*.swift, Package.swift, Package.resolved, gate/universal.sh|gate/universal.sh|-|-|the release binary is not arm64 + x86_64 with minos 14.0 in each slice (root T30, V6)
coverage|coverage|sherd|**/*.swift, Package.swift, .coverage, gate/coverage.sh|gate/coverage.sh|-|-|line coverage fell below the floor in .coverage (root V10)
flake-lock-graph|supply|jq|flake.lock|jq -e '[.nodes[] \| select(.locked.repo? == "nixpkgs")] \| length == 1' flake.lock|-|-|flake.lock holds more or fewer than one nixpkgs (paradigm/V20)
toolchain|supply|-|-|nix/toolchain-test.sh nix/toolchain.sh|-|-|the host toolchain is not Swift 6.2 or newer with XCTest, or the guard stopped refusing one (root V6, nix V1)
gen-check|gate|-|-|pklith gen --check|-|-|a step in hk.pklith.pkl no longer matches .pklith; run `pklith gen`
pklith-check|gate|-|-|pklith check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, or a row matches nothing
tdd-order|test|-|-|pklith check --pushed|-|-|a commit changed a file before its test; commit the test first or with it
no-stash|gate|gnugrep|-|! grep -nE 'stash *= *(true\|"git"\|"patch-file")' hk.pkl|-|-|hk.pkl stashes in a hook; parallel worktrees share git stash (paradigm/V15)
no-core-worktree|gate|git|-|test -z "$(git config --local --get core.worktree)"|-|-|core.worktree is set in the shared .git/config, so every worktree acts on one checkout (paradigm/V15)
names|gate|gnugrep|**/*|gate/names.sh {{files}}|-|-|a private name is staged (paradigm/V37); the hit names the denylist entry, never the name
bats-unit|test|openssl|-|bats --recursive gate release|-|-|a bats spec under gate/ or release/ failed (root T6, T23)
confirm|gate|-|-|pklith confirm|-|-|the gate is incomplete, stale, unrunnable or evaluates to no steps (paradigm/V22)
actlith-check|gate|-|-|actlith gen --check && actlith check|-|-|a workflow no longer matches .actlith, or a file in .github/workflows/ is neither generated nor listed hand-written; run `actlith gen` (root T14)

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker, no-local-paths, names, no-core-worktree|-|-
bats|bats-parse, bats-changed, bats-unit|-|-
actlith|actlith-check|-|-
Makefile|-|-|upstream build entry points, unchanged (root §F); no linter in the catalog reads them
commit-msg|shellcheck|-|-
context-limits|sherd-budget|-|-
coverage|coverage|-|-
editorconfig|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
envrc|shellcheck|-|-
gitattributes|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
gitignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no linter reads them
lock|flake-lock-graph|-|-
markdownlintignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no linter reads them
md|markdownlint|-|-
nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix|-|-
path:**/SPEC-ARCHIVE.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt|-|-
path:**/SPEC.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget|-|-
path:.github/actions/**|-|-|upstream composite action, untouched (root §C); the upstream workflows use it
path:.github/workflows/build-main.yml|-|-|upstream CI, untouched (root §C, D12); listed hand-written in .actlith
path:.github/workflows/build.yml|-|-|upstream CI, untouched (root §C, D12); listed hand-written in .actlith
path:.github/workflows/ci.yml|actionlint, zizmor, yamllint|-|-
path:.github/workflows/release.yml|-|-|upstream CI, untouched (root §C, D12); listed hand-written in .actlith
path:fixtures/*/*|-|-|fixture bytes written by upstream, frozen (fixtures V2): no linter reads keys, recipients or protocol transcripts; the * steps still read them, blank, newline and editorconfig steps skip them (hk.pkl)
path:Documentation/**|-|-|upstream man page and design notes, unchanged, not a node (root §F); not reformatted (D3)
path:README.md|-|-|upstream page, unchanged (D3); its trailing blanks are markdown line breaks; baseline in hk.pkl and .markdownlintignore (D13)
path:Scripts/**|-|-|upstream build and coverage scripts, unchanged, not a node (root §F); not reformatted (D3)
path:Sources/CLI.swift|-|-|upstream file whose help text literal ends lines in blanks (D3, root V11): trailing-whitespace and editorconfig-checker skip it (hk.pkl baseline, D13); every other step still reads it, nothing is claimed until upstream strips them
path:gate/*.sh|shellcheck, shfmt, bats-changed, bats-unit|-|-
path:nix/toolchain*.sh|shellcheck, shfmt, toolchain|-|-
path:release/*.bats|bats-parse, bats-changed, bats-unit|-|-
path:release/*.sh|shellcheck, shfmt, bats-changed, bats-unit|-|-
pkl|no-stash|-|-
pklith|gen-check, pklith-check, tdd-order, confirm|-|-
pre-commit|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-push|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
resolved|build, test, hardware, universal|-|-
secretsignore|-|-|ignore patterns and allowed strings, no linter reads them
sh|shellcheck, shfmt|-|-
swift|swift-format, build, test, hardware, universal, coverage|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
txt|-|-|license text, no linter reads it
yaml|yamllint|-|-
yml|yamllint|-|-

## rules
id|kind|select|target|except
swift-test|exists|Sources/*.swift|Tests/Fork/{stem}ForkTests.swift|-
swift-orphan|orphan|Tests/*Tests.swift|Sources/{stem\|chop:ForkTests\|chop:Tests}.swift|Tests/StanzaTests.swift
swift-tdd|tdd-order|Sources/*.swift|Tests/Fork/{stem}ForkTests.swift|-
gate-bats|exists|gate/*.sh|gate/{stem}.bats|-
release-bats|exists|release/*.sh|release/{stem}.bats|-
